      "title": "Faculty and Staff Programs & Committees",
      "description": "Faculty and Staff Programs & Committees Skip To Main Site Navigation Skip to Content Skip To Footer Close APPLY VISIT REQUEST INFO GIVE NEWS & EVENTS Submit ABOUT THE MOUNT Mission, Vision, Values History & Heritage Sponsorship Transition Campus Icons & Traditions Mount Moments University Leadership Campus Facilities ACADEMICS Find Your Program Career Center Academic Support Co-ops & Internships Honors Program Service Learning Study Abroad Archbishop Alter Library Registrar ADMISSION & AID Undergraduate First-Year Admissions Undergraduate Adult Admissions Graduate Admissions International Admissions Transfer Admissions Veteran & Military Admissions Orientation & New Student Events Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Payments & Billing ATHLETICS msjlions.com Esports Intramurals Joe Lion Mascot Program ENRICHMENT PROGRAMS Art Guild Band Choir Lions First Scholars Mission Ambassadors Mosaic Scholars Theatre Arts Video Production Writer's Block STUDENT EXPERIENCE Living on Campus Campus Dining Life in Cincinnati Campus Ministry Student Involvement & Clubs Health & Wellness Campus Safety Commencement Quick Links Majors Alumni & Friends Directory Employment Opportunities Media Relations Parent & Family Resources The ROAR Store Title IX Virtual Tour We use cookies to ensure we give you the best user experience. By continuing to use this site, we will\n                assume\n                you agree to the use of cookies. Privacy Policy Accept × Apply VISIT Request Info Give Visit Apply Faculty and Staff Programs & Committees Home Employment at the University Faculty and Staff Programs Faculty and Staff Programs & Committees Faculty & Staff Committees Mount St. Joseph University Council on Belonging Excellence The Council for Belonging Excellence serves as an advisory committee to help guide The Center for Mission & Belonging staff on strategies to further the Mount’s mission and social justice. The Council is comprised of representatives from across campus, alumni, and friends within the Greater Cincinnati Community.  Specifically, the Council provides advice related to actions, policies, and procedures that promote and maintain a culture of belonging, respect, and care for all persons in the Mount Community. Professional Allies Group Professional Allies is comprised of faculty and staff who meet each month and actively discuss and create avenues to support the LBGTQIA+ community at the Mount. Faculty and Staff Programs Mission Orientation Program Information and Registration During Convocation Week in August all new faculty and staff hired in the last 12-months enjoy a morning together as we learn about and reflect on the Mount's mission. The morning ends with a wonderful lunch hosted by President and Mrs. Williams in their home. Be sure to join us! Registration will begin in July. What People are Saying about Mission Orientation Thorough representation of how the history of MSJ translates into our purpose today. Welcoming/ intentional The event was well put-together and efficient! Content pacing and variety was great, and a half-day is enough without being too little or too much. A reminder that a purpose filled life is filled with learning and service. Community: MSJ's Mission Immersion Motivating! FUN! Amazing insightful Inspiring Informative Inspirational Missional interactive, time with the Sisters, variety in speakers Organization and pace, content and connecting to the sisters A reminder that vocations are deeper than careers, and that this organization has purpose. Community! I loved the authenticity & vulnerability of our speakers. Passion, personal Well organized, light hearted, fun, educational, inspiring. Spark Sessions Fall Session 1  - Oct. 1, 2025 Join Joe and Katrice for an MSJ commUNITY learning session designed to spark our imaginations and ignite our shared vision about the impact we want to make in students' lives. These sessions will be an opportunity to connect, be inspired, and create Mount moments that matter as we rise to new heights! Who should attend? faculty and staff who have energy to take things to the next level faculty and staff who are exhausted and are looking to be inspired faculty and staff who want to connect with others and are curious about what makes certain moments extraordinary Fall Session 2 - Oct. 29, 2025 The next Spark Session will be: Wednesday, October 29 from Noon -1 p.m. in the Clifford Room Join Joe and Katrice for an MSJ commUNITY learning session designed to spark our imaginations and ignite our shared vision about the impact we want to make in students' lives. These sessions will be an opportunity to connect, be inspired, and create Mount moments that matter as we rise to new heights! Who should attend? faculty and staff who have energy to take things to the next level faculty and staff who are exhausted and are looking to be inspired faculty and staff who want to connect with others and are curious about what makes certain moments extraordinary What people said about the last Spark Session: Fun! Fun, light hearted Fun time Insightful Intriguing Fun, Connecting, Creative Connections Helped me think differently than I do in my typical day Great job with team building and getting people to think and work together Looking forward to the next session Made me want to come back Please continue these. Hope to encourage more to attend. Thank you, this helped me clear my head and now I have energy to get back to grading… Click Here to Register Why do Catholics do That? Why do Catholics do that during Advent and Christmas? Join Joe Shadle as we learn about the origins of many of our Advent and Christmas traditions including: Who invented the Advent wreath? When did we start using Christmas trees? Who came up with the idea for the Advent calendar? Why do we use red and green, holly, and poinsettias during the Christmas season? Who was St. Nicholas? Was Jesus born on December 25th? How many \"wise men\" were there and do we know their names? Whose idea was the Nativity Scene? Registration will begin in November Mount St. Joseph University 5701 Delhi Road, Cincinnati, OH 45233-1670 1-800-654-9314 Policies & Disclosures Title IX E-Verify, Equal Opportunity and Non-Discrimination Privacy Policy Accessibility Services Consumer Information Group Health Plan MRF Terms of Use Campus Resources MountConnect Portal Campus Map Contact Us Employment Frequently Asked Questions Virtual Tour © Mount St. Joseph University, All Rights Reserved"
